:1,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What happened\n\nOpening claude-config #27 created the issue and linked its parent, then failed: 'failed: GraphQL: Content already exists in this project (addProjectV2ItemById)', with 'not completed: added new issue to board; set new issue Status Backlog', and the command exited with an error.\n\n### What I expected\n\nThe issue ends up on its board with Status Backlog and the command succeeds, whether the tool or the board's auto-add rule adds it first.\n\n### How to reproduce\n\nOpen an issue with tools/workflow/issue.py open in a repository whose board has an auto-add rule for it, such as claude-config on Tooling (board 2). Since 2026-10-26 every repository has one. GitHub's rule and the tool race to add the issue, and the tool fails whenever the rule wins. Opening #26 earlier the same day worked because the tool won.\n\n### Where\n\ntools/workflow/issue.py, board_add() and its callers in open_issue(), for the new issue and for strays. Found landing G9a.\n\n### Done when\n\nWhen adding an issue to its board fails because the issue is already on that board, open finds the existing card, sets Status Backlog and succeeds; when the issue really isn't on the board, it still reports the failure.\n","closed_by":{"login":"sh4i-yurei","id":232996764,"node_id":"U_kgDODeM_nA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232996764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei","html_url":"https://github.com/sh4i-yurei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sh4i-yurei/subscriptions","organiza